In article <93332.102723DVL@psuvm.psu.edu>, Roger Christman <DVL@psuvm.psu.edu> writes:
|> Something I really don't understand.
|> I play a perfectly ordinary game and then save when I get to
|> level 7.  In between I patch up my NETHACK.CNF to fix a few
|> options.  When I come back, it tells me the "save file is out of date"
|> 
|> Doesn't it seem odd that just playing with the CNF should do this?
|> But it gets even better:
|> 
|> I experimented a little more.  I entered a game, and as Action 1,
|> just Saved.  I immediately turn around, and try to play the same
|> game, and once again, the "save file is out of date"
|> 
|> What gives?
|> For anyone who cares, this is 3.1.3 running on a 640K 286 clone.

Check you system clock.  Also check that the date on the nethack executable is
not 'in the future' WRT the system clock.  If the save file is older than the
executable or newer than the current time, it assumes that it's out of date.

